# One Music Generation Engine

Part of platform **Single Source of Truth** — see [single-source-of-truth.mdc](./single-source-of-truth.mdc).

## Platform principle

We are building **one central musical generation engine**, not separate generators per page. Every creative feature uses the same engine; **pages differ only in purpose and constraints**.

Improve the engine once → Missions, Phrase & Motif, Composition Studio, Practice, and AI Coach examples all improve automatically.

## Engine owns (single implementation)

- Musical phrase generation
- Rhythm generation
- Difficulty scaling (level + easier/harder relative tiers)
- Theory (via `music_theory`: normalize, classify, chord tones, targets, scales)
- Key-signature spelling (`spell_note_in_key`)
- Chord-tone / target-note selection for generated lines
- Sheet music (ABC), guitar TAB, MIDI, playback hooks

## Canonical modules

| Role | Module |
|------|--------|
| Public facade | `motif_engine.py` — `generate_musical_phrase`, re-exports |
| Core engine | `improvisation_motif.py` |
| Mission constraints | `improvisation_mission_rules.py` |
| Theory / playback token separation | `music_theory.py`, `.cursor/rules/theory-playback-separation.mdc` |

Full plan: `cursor-prompts/plans/2026-07-31-unified-motif-engine-and-coaching-profile.md`

## Pages = goals, not generators

### Missions — teach one concept

Mission text **defines constraints** passed to the engine (after base phrase generation).

Examples: chord tones only, guide tones, target 9ths, rhythmic variation, motif development, dominant tension, beat-1 resolution.

Generated examples must **demonstrate the selected Mission**.

### Phrase & Motif — idea generator

Creative exploration on the same engine: New / Harder / Easier motif; future stylistic intents (more lyrical, rhythmic, bluesy, jazz vocabulary, continue idea, contrasting idea).

**Transform tools** (invert, sequence up/down, rhythmic variation) operate on the **active motif** regardless of how it was generated.

### Composition Studio — write songs

Migrate from parallel text-only `motif_hint` paths to **songwriting constraints** on the same engine.

Examples: verse melody, chorus hook, bridge, singable range, hook repeat, pre-chorus tension, style/harmony fit.

### AI Coach — analyze first, generate when teaching

Primary workflow:

`Student recording → performance analysis → coaching feedback`

Use the engine **only when the coach needs an example** (“here’s a better guide-tone line”, “a motif that demonstrates today’s Mission”). The coach analyzes; the engine illustrates.

### Practice — performance-oriented examples

Example lines via engine with practice-appropriate constraints (not a separate generator).

## Coaching UX (separate from generation)

| Page | Role |
|------|------|
| **AI Improvisation Metrics & AI** | Long-term **coaching profile** (skills, strictness, tone, depth, goals) — persists weeks/months |
| **Mission Upload Analysis** | **Today’s performance review** — mission completion, strengths, fixes, next steps; **inherits** global profile for weighting and voice |

Do not duplicate metric multiselect on both pages; profile + today’s mission merge at analysis time.

## Do not

- Add new standalone phrase/motif generators in page UI or Composition modules
- Parse playback tokens for theory (use `normalize_chord_for_theory`)
- Show musician-facing note names without key-signature spelling
- Make AI Coach a music generator — analysis first, engine as teaching tool

## When adding features

1. Extend `improvisation_motif` / `motif_engine` for generation behavior.
2. Add a **constraint module or parameters** for the page goal (mission rules, composition recipe, coach example request).
3. Keep UI as a view over engine output (notation, TAB, playback).
